;; day8/re-frame2-fresco — the Fresco view substrate.
;;
;; Fresco is a lean-React substrate: a boundary is a real React function
;; component minted by `defview`, and the runtime owns exactly the three
;; things React does not — which boundaries a commit must re-run, how a
;; body reaches subscription values, and the fence that keeps one render
;; pass on one commit. The public door is `re-frame.fresco`; everything
;; else is `re-frame.fresco.impl.*` and is not a consumer surface.
;;
;; The measured prototype this artefact is derived from is evidence at
;; bench/fresco/ (repo root), its own hand-run project off this classpath;
;; nothing here may require it, and
;; `scripts/check_optional_module_reachability.py` is what checks that.
;;
;; DEPENDENCIES. Core, plus ssr for the server module alone. Every substrate
;; namespace the RUNTIME reaches for — `re-frame.adapter.context`,
;; `re-frame.live-frame`, `re-frame.late-bind`, `re-frame.registrar`,
;; `re-frame.performance`, `re-frame.trace`, `re-frame.interop` — is core's,
;; and routing is reached through core's late-bind registry rather than by
;; dependency, so the packaging graph stays `fresco -> core late-bind
;; <- routing` with no cycle (Conventions §Packaging). React itself is an
;; npm dependency, declared in implementation/package.json, not here.
;;
;; `day8/re-frame2-ssr` is reached by ONE namespace, `re-frame.fresco.server`,
;; which the public door names nowhere.
;; The module hands `:payload` to `re-frame.ssr.payload-policy`'s
;; fail-closed validator and its app-db to that namespace's own egress
;; projection, so R0 — *nothing Fresco-specific touches the payload path*
;; — is a packaging fact rather than a promise; re-spelling those three
;; helpers locally to keep the dep list at one entry is precisely how the
;; wire contract drifts. `ssr` itself depends on core alone, so the graph
;; is the DAG `fresco -> ssr -> core`.
;;
;; It costs a CLASSPATH entry and no bundle bytes: a browser build that
;; never requires `re-frame.fresco.server` reaches no `re-frame.ssr`
;; namespace, which is the same optional-module property `.forms`,
;; `.overlay` and `.motion` have and which
;; `scripts/check_optional_module_reachability.py` checks at the door.
;;
;; PUBLISHED. The `:clein/build` alias below carries the
;; Maven coordinate `day8/re-frame2-fresco`, and the artefact is enrolled in
;; `.github/scripts/verify-version-lockstep.sh`'s inventory and in
;; `.github/workflows/release.yml`'s deploy DAG. It is NOT a `deploy-leaf`
;; matrix value: the `:deps` above name a SECOND in-repo artefact besides core
;; (`day8/re-frame2-ssr`), which is the exact property that put `ssr-ring` in
;; a post-matrix stage of its own — under the matrix's `fail-fast: false` such
;; a leaf can publish a pom naming a coordinate whose own deploy is red, and
;; Clojars has no yank. So Fresco ships from `deploy-fresco`, gated on the
;; whole matrix succeeding, and `implementation/scripts/_release-dag-policy.test.cjs`
;; asserts that ordering from the workflow's real job graph rather than by
;; convention.
;;
;; `:src-dirs` carries `resources` as well as `src`, for the reason `:paths`
;; does: the clj-kondo export reaches a consumer over the CLASSPATH, so a jar
;; without it silently ships no lint layer at all.
;;
;; IT ALSO CARRIES `test_kit/src`, WHICH `:paths` DOES NOT. The two
;; keys are not the same lever and this artefact is the one place they diverge:
;; `:paths` is the classpath a `:local/root` consumer inherits, while `:src-dirs`
;; is the ONLY thing that decides jar content — clein's `create-jar` is
;; `copy-src` then `b/jar`, and `copy-src` is `b/copy-dir` over
;; `(concat :src-dirs :resource-dirs)` into `:class-dir`, so a root that is off
;; `:src-dirs` is off the jar and nothing else puts it back. Were the kit off
;; `:src-dirs`, a `v*` tag would publish a `day8/re-frame2-fresco` containing no
;; `re-frame.fresco.test` and no `re-frame.fresco.test.mounted` — the supported
;; testing surface, absent from the artefact that documents it, with no second
;; coordinate to get it from.
;;
;; This does NOT weaken the kit's dev-only property, because that property is
;; not the separate root's to give. `re-frame.fresco.evidence` and
;; `re-frame.fresco.tool` ship from `src/` and are dev-only by REACHABILITY —
;; no `src/` namespace requires them, so a consumer who never asks for the
;; projection never bundles a byte of it — and `scripts/check_production_erasure.cjs`
;; is what checks that, by scanning the release bundle for each surface's
;; sentinel. The kit is on that same roster, under the sentinel
;; `rf.error/fresco-test-`, and its entry states the real rule: no
;; `src/` namespace may require the kit. A classpath entry costs no bundle bytes;
;; a `:require` does. The kit is off `:paths`, so the in-repo lane and the
;; `:local/root` route ask for it explicitly.
;;
;; `resources` is on :paths for ONE reason: the clj-kondo export
;; reaches a consumer over the CLASSPATH. `clj-kondo --lint
;; "$(clojure -Spath)" --dependencies --copy-configs` scans the classpath for
;; `clj-kondo.exports/<group>/<artifact>/`, so an export directory that is not
;; on :paths is simply invisible — and the failure mode is silence rather than
;; an error. `scripts/check_lint_export.py` asserts this line rather than
;; trusting it.
;; Nothing under `resources/` is a loadable namespace: the hook file is data
;; that clj-kondo's own SCI reads from the config directory.
{:paths ["src" "resources"]
 :deps  {day8/re-frame2     {:local/root "../core"}
         day8/re-frame2-ssr {:local/root "../ssr"}}

 :aliases
 ;; The runtime requires React, so nearly every suite `re-frame.fresco.*`
 ;; writes is CLJS and runs on the Node lane (`re-frame.fresco.*-cljs-test`,
 ;; compiled by the `:node-test-fresco` shadow-cljs build). The one exception
 ;; is what this lane runs: `test/re_frame/fresco/slot_cljs_test.cljc` is the
 ;; `.cljc` equivalence pin for the canonical slot rule, asserted once in Node
 ;; and once on the JVM against ONE implementation (`impl/slot.cljc`). So the
 ;; lane takes the runner's test-count floor rather than a `--probe`
 ;; exemption: 3 tests, and the runner refuses if that ever becomes 0.
 ;;
 ;; THE JVM ARM IS GATED, ON EVERY PR. The artefact is on
 ;; `scripts/test-jvm-implementation.sh`'s roster, and
 ;; `.github/workflows/test.yml` runs `jvm-fresco` unconditionally, in
 ;; `all-required-passed`'s `needs:`. `check_jvm_lane_rosters.py` holds the
 ;; two together: R1 refuses a roster entry with no CI job and R2 a gated
 ;; job with no roster entry, so an entry and its job land in one change.
 ;;
 ;; The lint export's witness is NOT a JVM suite. It is
 ;; `scripts/check_lint_export.py`, run by `npm run test:fresco-lint` — a
 ;; checker over the package, the same shape as `check_guide_samples.py`.
 {:test {:extra-paths ["test"
                       ;; `re-frame.fresco.test`, the supported
                       ;; L0–L2 testing surface. Its own root, and NOT in
                       ;; `:paths` above, so the in-repo lane and any
                       ;; `:local/root` consumer ask for it by name. It IS on
                       ;; `:clein/build`'s `:src-dirs`, so the published jar
                       ;; carries it — see the `:src-dirs` paragraph
                       ;; in the header for why those are different levers and
                       ;; why a classpath entry is not a bundle byte. Listed
                       ;; here so the classpath probe sees it; the CLJS lane
                       ;; reaches it through the `fresco/test_kit/src`
                       ;; :source-paths entry in implementation/shadow-cljs.edn.
                       "test_kit/src"]
         :extra-deps  {day8/re-frame2-test-quiet {:local/root "../test-quiet"}
                       ;; The Node lane's substrate. The package's
                       ;; node-lane suites run on the UIx adapter and not on
                       ;; plain-atom, because plain-atom has no reactivity
                       ;; layer — a subscription under it never notifies, so
                       ;; every commit assertion would pass vacuously by
                       ;; never firing. Test-only: shipping source names no
                       ;; adapter at all.
                       day8/re-frame2-uix {:local/root "../adapters/uix"}}
         :main-opts   ["-m" "re-frame.test-quiet.runner"]}

  ;; clj-kondo as a JVM dep, so the lint-export gate needs no native binary
  ;; install — the same shape the deps-new template ships for a consumer app
  ;; (`tools/template/resources/.../deps.edn`). PINNED to the version
  ;; `.github/workflows/lint.yml` installs: two clj-kondo versions disagree
  ;; about which findings are errors, so a gate that asserts on findings must
  ;; assert about the build the project actually gates on.
  :clj-kondo
  {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version "2026.04.15"}}
   :main-opts  ["-m" "clj-kondo.main"]}

  ;; Clojars deploy. The release workflow swaps both
  ;; :local/root coordinates above for :mvn/version before invoking clein,
  ;; on the throwaway runner checkout.
  :clein {:extra-deps {io.github.noahtheduke/clein
                       {:git/url "https://github.com/day8/clein.git"
                        :git/sha "2b83503246e8291fc023d688574640a9b23d8c50"}}
          :main-opts  ["-m" "noahtheduke.clein"]}

  :clein/build
  {:lib      day8/re-frame2-fresco
   :main     re-frame.fresco
   :url      "https://github.com/day8/re-frame2"
   :version  "../../VERSION"
   :license  {:name "MIT"
              :url  "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT"}
   :src-dirs ["src" "resources" "test_kit/src"]}}}
